 "issue": 1777,
 "issue_title": "Bug: clarify unregister_step error for built-in Python steps",
 "issue_body": "## Summary\n`unregister_step()` reports built-in Python-backed pipeline steps as unknown instead of explaining that built-in steps cannot be unregistered.\n\n## Why it matters\n`list_steps()` shows steps such as `filter_rows`, `replace_values`, `safe_divide_columns`, and `standardize_missing_tokens` as available. If a user tries to unregister one, the current error says the step is unknown, which is confusing for contributors and users debugging pipeline registry state.\n\n## Evidence\n- `arnio/pipeline.py`: `unregister_step()` checks `_PYTHON_STEP_REGISTRY`, then raises `UnknownStepError` for built-in Python-backed steps detected by `_is_builtin_python_step()`.\n- `arnio/pipeline.py`: `list_steps()` includes both `_STEP_REGISTRY` and `_PYTHON_STEP_REGISTRY`, so these names are visibly available.\n- Reproduced on current `origin/main` by importing the checkout and running `ar.unregister_step(\"filter_rows\")`.\n\n## Reproduction or trigger\n1. Import Arnio from current `main`.\n2. Confirm `\"filter_rows\" in ar.list_steps()`.\n3. Run `ar.unregister_step(\"filter_rows\")`.\n\n## Expected behavior\nThe error should clearly say that built-in Arnio steps cannot be unregistered, and ideally suggest unregistering only custom user-registered steps.\n\n## Actual behavior\nThe call raises `UnknownStepError: Unknown pipeline step: 'filter_rows'.`, even though `filter_rows` is present in `list_steps()`.\n\n## Suggested direction\nAdd a dedicated validation branch in `unregister_step()` for built-in Python-backed steps and raise a clearer `ValueError`/custom Arnio error. Add tests for `filter_rows`, `replace_values`, and a truly missing custom step so the messages stay distinct.\n\n## References\n- `arnio/pipeline.py`\n- `tests/test_pipeline.py`\r\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/1777",
 "pr": 2252,
 "pr_title": "Prevent unregistering built-in Python steps",
